00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:41,840
as a very loose analogy, I do find it interesting to note.

100
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:46,960
Anyway, the third way that we can help increase this neuron's activation is by changing all

101
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:51,960
the activations in the previous layer, namely if everything connected to that digit two

102
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:56,600
neuron with a positive weight got brighter, and if everything connected with a negative

103
00:06:56,600 --> 00:07:02,600
weight got dimmer, then that digit two neuron would become more active.

104
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:06,160
And similar to the weight changes, you're going to get the most bang for your buck by

105
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:10,880
seeking changes that are proportional to the size of the corresponding weights.

106
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:15,400
Now, of course, we cannot directly influence those activations.

