00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:40,360
There's kind of a lot going on here, so let's just sum it up for ourselves, shall we?

157
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:45,440
Track propagation is the algorithm for determining how a single training example would like to

158
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:50,000
nudge the weights and biases, not just in terms of whether they should go up or down,

159
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:54,760
