163
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:09,120
But that's computationally slow, so instead you randomly subdivide the data into these

164
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:14,000
mini-batches and compute each step with respect to a mini-batch.

165
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,560
Repeatedly going through all of the mini-batches and making these adjustments, you will converge

166
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:23,040
towards a local minimum of the cost function, which is to say your network is going to end

167
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:27,480
up doing a really good job on the training examples.

